[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main Modules

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
HVPS Bootloader Firmware - The firmware is stored at the base memory address on the microcontroller
and facilitates the loading of new HVPS Interface firmware (.hex) files in the remaining
flash memory.

HVPS Bootloader PC Application - This app offers a desktop GUI that loads the HVPS Interface
firmware at the location in memory specified and managed by the bootloader. The GUI allows the
selection of a COM port that corresponds to the USB port established by the bootloader.

Flash Memory - Where the bootloader firmware is stored and new HVPS Interface firmware is flashed.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-11
TITLE: Application Program Handling
STATEMENT: >>>
At the beginning of bootloader firmware execution, the program parses the predetermined application
region in flash memory and calculates a CRC over the complete region. The application firmware build
calculates and stores the programmed CRC over that same region, treating unprogrammed bytes as erased
flash. The bootloader compares its calculated CRC to the programmed CRC in the designated storage
location. If the values match, the bootloader considers the application valid and jumps to the
application firmware for execution.

If the calculated value does not match the stored value, then the firmware will not jump to the
application for execution but will instead wait for PC communication for commands to update the
application memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-13
TITLE: Flash Memory Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware can both erase and write to the flash memory of the microcontroller. The physical flash
erase pages are 2048 bytes in size. When the firmware receives an erase command from the PC, it
erases 91 physical pages in the region pre-designated for application memory. The firmware derives
this erase count by dividing the configured application-page limit of 180 by two and adding one.

Each PC write command provides a 256-byte payload and an application-relative sub-page index. The
firmware accepts indices from 0 through 180 and rejects greater indices. It calculates the destination
from the application start address and the index, then programs the payload word by word as 32-bit
values.

The flash memory controller for the microcontroller requires that the firmware lock and unlock the
flash memory for manipulation, as a way to protect against unwanted corruption of the flash
memory. When performing erase and write procedures, the firmware will appropriately unlock and
lock the flash memory controller peripheral of the microcontroller.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-3
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-12
TITLE: Manufacturer Hardware Abstraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates source code provided by the manufacturer of the microcontroller unit in
order to interface with various peripherals of the microcontroller. These include functions to
interface with the following peripherals of the microcontroller:

- UART serial port
- GPIO
- Flash memory controller
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
